{
 "title": "Animation basics: keyframes and a loop",
 "summary": "Keyframes (I) on the timeline at 24 fps: a cube scaled in Y at frame 40 and Z at 80 and back at 120 (frame 1's key duplicated), a sphere moving and returning, a Suzanne's material keyed blue and rough at frame 1 and red and glossy at 120. Then the loop animation: a squashed cylinder base with four pockets cut by a Boolean (four cylinders joined), bevelled; four balls in the pockets; a stand and a rod turned 45 degrees. Over 60 frames the rod turns 180 one way and the base 180 the other; the balls jump (up about 1 m, held a moment) over the rod and land in the next pockets twice a loop. Materials from the library (car paint base, dark metal stand, brushed aluminium rod, four copies of glossy green painted recoloured), a dark floor, rendered portrait 1080 x 1920.",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "LoopBase",
   "description": "the base"
  },
